-
-## Performance and accessibility
-
-- Gallery covers use local CSS and SVG instead of nine simultaneous canvases.
-- The demo groups are dynamically imported when needed.
-- Only the open spatial demo renders continuously; the hero pauses while the
-  dialog is open. Offscreen/hidden-tab rendering is paused, and DPR is capped.
-- Three.js geometry, particles and studio lighting are procedural and local.
-- Scene resources and listeners are cleaned up when components unmount.
-- Reduced-motion preferences and the gallery's motion toggle are respected.
-- A native modal dialog provides focus trapping, Escape handling and an inert
-  background. Focus returns to the opener. Lenis is paused without blocking
-  native scrolling inside the dialog.
-- Drag interactions have button, keyboard or status-menu alternatives.
-- Loading/import failures expose a retry action. Clipboard failure exposes
-  selectable text instead of silently claiming success.
-- WebGL2 availability is checked before creating a renderer. On unsupported
-  browsers or context loss, an illustrated fallback remains usable. GPU-only
-  controls are disabled honestly; supported preview controls remain available.
-
-## Verification
-
-The implementation was production-built with the repository's existing lockfile
-and inspected in the browser. Desktop checks covered category filters, both
-locales, all nine dialogs, representative interactions, Escape and focus return.
